# 30. TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION STANDARDS

Use Luau and supported Roblox APIs.

Requirements:

- Use proper type annotations where practical.
- Use clear names and comments.
- Avoid deprecated APIs.
- Use task.wait, task.spawn, and other appropriate task-library methods instead of deprecated alternatives.
- Handle asynchronous operations correctly.
- Use pcall where appropriate for networked services and persistent data operations.
- Avoid blocking the entire game while loading player data.
- Separate server logic from client presentation.
- Centralize tunable values.
- Avoid unnecessary duplication.
- Use CollectionService tags or attributes where they improve maintainability.
- Document module dependencies.
- Ensure required RemoteEvents and RemoteFunctions are created or provide a reliable setup script.
- Validate all referenced instances and configurations.
- Make initialization order explicit.
- Handle missing assets gracefully.

Every script must include its intended location and purpose.

Every remote must have a documented argument schema and validation rules.

Do not provide pseudocode when working executable Luau code is reasonably possible.

If an implementation cannot be completed, identify the exact missing dependency and provide the best working fallback.

