# 31. TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

Before declaring the project complete, verify the following or provide an explicit manual test procedure if automated execution is unavailable.

ROUND SYSTEM:
- Two players can start a round.
- The round ends correctly.
- The server returns everyone to the lobby.
- Players leaving mid-round do not break the system.
- New rounds can start repeatedly.

MONSTER:
- The Copy can spawn.
- It can imitate a player.
- It can investigate noises.
- It can pursue a valid target.
- It can lose a target.
- It can recover from failed pathfinding.
- It does not become permanently stuck.

OBJECTIVES:
- Required items spawn correctly.
- Objectives update for all players.
- Objective rewards cannot be duplicated.
- The exit unlocks only when requirements are satisfied.

BLACKOUTS:
- Lights restore correctly.
- Events do not overlap incorrectly.
- Temporary objects are cleaned up.

PROGRESSION:
- Rewards are calculated server-side.
- Valid data saves and loads.
- Data failures are handled safely.

GAMEPASSES:
- Real configured IDs trigger the Roblox purchase prompt.
- Unconfigured IDs do not trigger fake success.
- Ownership is refreshed after purchase.
- Owned passes display correctly.
- Server-side perks require verified ownership.

UI:
- Desktop controls work.
- Mobile controls work.
- UI fits common screen sizes.
- The shop can be opened and closed.
- Results and objectives remain readable.

SECURITY:
- Invalid objective claims are rejected.
- Invalid reward requests are rejected.
- Remote spam is rate-limited.
- Spectators cannot alter active gameplay.

PERFORMANCE:
- No obvious unbounded loops.
- No accumulating temporary monsters or event objects.
- No repeated round initialization leaks.
- Reasonable performance with six players.

Do not claim these tests passed unless they have actually been executed.

